# The assessment of CHK-003 against this build. The requirement identifier is this
# file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the
# identity is a second place for it to be wrong — the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a
# record registration, for the same reason.
#
# CHK-003 requires that every run report evaluated, excluded, unsupported, unavailable,
# failed, not-applicable and agent-required combinations. `Applicability` answered six of
# the seven and had no state for agent-required; OD-CONTRACTS-002 decided the seventh and
# P10-AGENT-REQUIRED built it. That record is also where the argument that CHK-003 binds
# this build at all is made, which is why it is named here rather than merely cited.
#
# Authored from OD-CONTRACTS-002's assessment, which was itself authored against
# NOMOS_V14_CORPUS. It is not recomputed from the corpus at check time, and OD-TRACE-001
# records why: CI has no corpus, so a guard that read one would be green by being unable
# to look.
